description:
Context: flywheel-teams lets a person run the agent flywheel (Claude Code and Codex swarms under ntm or frankenterm, with beads, Agent Mail and dcg) in repositories that other people also work in, without changing how the flywheel works for that person and without changing the repository for the other people. Three situations: a repository the operator does not own whose team has not adopted the flywheel (the operator overlay, M1); a repository the team owns where several people run the flywheel (team mode, M3); and the transitions between them. Principle (Ryan, 2026-10-24): once the overlay is installed and its config confirmed in a repository, running the flywheel there is just like running the flywheel anywhere.

Plan of record: docs/plans/2026-11-09-flywheel-teams.md (v1.1). AGENTS.md is the contract for working here: bash 3.2 plus jq only, shellcheck clean, every behaviour with a test and a planted negative under test/, no em dashes, nothing that names a client. This repository is public.

Why: the guarantees should be evidence, not configuration, and new tooling folders, a half-filled template or a reset core.hooksPath must be noticed before a swarm starts. Plan section 6.7.

fwt doctor [<repo>] [--json] checks and reports each as pass, fail or info:
- each overlay file exists and is current (hashes match);
- the generated file plus ~/.codex/AGENTS.md plus any instruction file in a parent directory is no larger than project_doc_max_bytes as configured in ~/.codex/config.toml (Codex applies the limit to the combined bytes);
- excludes in place; no untracked, unignored top-level dot path;
- .beads/ tracked or ready to commit, with README and attributes;
- the guard installed (install.sh --check) and the packs enabled through .dcg.toml as configured;
- the git hooks are ours, and core.hooksPath still points at the wrapper directory when one was installed (husky's prepare resets it on npm install);
- the current branch is the trunk;
- no applying Claude settings file sets pluginConfigs."cc-plugin-agents-md@builtin".options.instructionFiles to claude-md-and-agents-md, which would load the generated AGENTS.md beside CLAUDE.local.md;
- no {{PLACEHOLDER}} or <!-- fwt: --> marker left in the doctrine; the version key spelling;
- version stamps in generated files and hooks match the running fwt;
- the fetched default branch does not add an instruction file the overlay generates (else: run fwt sync --rename before pulling);
- whether frankenterm is installed (info) and, if so, that .ft/ and ft.toml are excluded;
- whether the default branch has platform-side protection (info, via gh api when gh is on PATH and authenticated; "not checked" otherwise);
- jq present and the guard's config files parse (the guard fails open without them).

Exit codes: 0 healthy, 1 findings, 2 could not run. --json emits one object per check with name, status, detail and fix. Also wires the final doctor call at the end of fwt init.

Tests (test/doctor.test.sh): a healthy repository; one broken fixture per check; the husky shape with core.hooksPath reset; JSON schema stable. Negative control: a mutant that reports pass for a missing CLAUDE.local.md must be caught.

Depends on install.sh, the packs, init and sync, and the gate.
